# The jars the Java client is built and run against, pinned by fingerprint.
#
# A8 compares Kafka's official client with ours, so which build of that client ran is part of the
# result. build.sh fetches these and refuses to go on where a fingerprint does not match, so a jar
# that changed under us stops the build rather than quietly producing a different experiment.
#
# Fingerprints are SHA-256 of the file as downloaded. Verify by hand with:
#   cd harness/java && sha256sum -c DEPENDENCIES
#
# kafka-clients 3.9.0 is Kafka's own producer and consumer, the thing A8 is about.
# slf4j-api 1.7.36 is the logging interface kafka-clients compiles against; with no binding on the
# classpath it prints one warning and discards its logs, which is what we want: a logging backend
# on the sending thread would be a second client inside the client.

